  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best result is RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200 (config_006, acc 0.653), while the only image-only test (config_010, resnet50) scored very poorly (0.208). This raises a critical uncertainty: is the image modality fundamentally uninformative, or was resnet50 simply an inadequate encoder? Question: config_013 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) isolates the effect of upgrading the image encoder from a small CNN to a large pretrained ViT, directly comparable to config_010. Why this is the best next experiment: Before committing limited budget to any of the 36 multimodal configurations, we need to know whether a stronger image encoder can produce a viable image representation. If imagenet_vit_l image-only is still very weak (<0.35), multimodal fusion is unlikely to beat the 0.653 RNA-only baseline and remaining budget should focus on RNA-only refinements. If it reaches ~0.5+, multimodal fusion becomes a high-value direction. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design axis (unimodal vs. multimodal) before any fusion experiments are run."
}

